---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../content';
const path = '/alternatives/marsello-alternative';
const title = "Marsello alternatives: retain the benefits, change the right layer";
const desc = "Decide whether to repair messaging, replace a channel, or move the loyalty program while honoring online and POS member benefits.";
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "When should we keep Marsello?",
    "answer": "Keep it when the supported POS and online loyalty program, staff process and marketing workflow serve the store well. Repair incorrect identity, earning rules or campaign ownership before replacing a working benefits system."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can a customer export move the whole loyalty program?",
    "answer": "Do not assume so. Reconcile balances, tier membership, earned and issued rewards, expiry and refund adjustments separately. Demonstrate the receiving system and a customer service fallback before retiring access."
  },
  {
    "question": "Does another SMS sender replace Marsello loyalty?",
    "answer": "A sender changes message execution. It does not establish equivalent earning, redemption, tiers or POS support. A partial replacement needs an agreed benefit source and one owner for each message queue."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} dateModified="2026-11-25" />
  <section class="container py-16">
    <a class="link" href="/alternatives">All alternatives</a>
    <p class="badge mt-6">Replacement decisions · November 25, 2026</p>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-5">{title}</h1>
    <p class="mt-7 text-xl leading-9">{desc}</p>
  </section>
  <article class="container prose-shopify pb-16">
    <h2>Start with what would be lost</h2>
    <p>Marsello can be a useful incumbent for a retailer whose online and physical-store purchases feed one loyalty experience. Its <a class="link" href="https://www.marsello.com/shopify">Shopify integration page</a> describes connected ecommerce and POS loyalty. The reason to stay is a working customer promise: staff recognize a member, explain the balance and redeem the right benefit. A more specialized campaign tool is attractive only if the missing messaging job is worth the additional handoff.</p>
    <p>Classify the problem from actual support tickets and workflow traces. Incorrect points after returns calls for loyalty-rule repair; duplicate reminders call for queue ownership repair. A channel execution gap may justify replacing only that channel. Full replacement is a different project, with member obligations, register training and benefit reconciliation as acceptance criteria. Store revenue alone selects none of these paths.</p>
    <h2>Create a retained benefit ledger before comparing candidates</h2>
    <p>Inventory each member identifier, source order, eligible spend, points entry, manual adjustment, reward issued, redemption and expiry. Record the tier qualification basis and period separately from the current points balance. Preserve the terms promised when the benefit was earned, the location allowed to honor it and the staff escalation owner. An outstanding reward is an obligation to resolve, not simply a segment label to copy.</p>
    <p>Marsello’s <a class="link" href="https://help.marsello.com/vip-tiers-program-common-questions-marsello-help-center">VIP tier FAQ</a> says the standard customer export does not include VIP tier, while tier segments can be exported. That makes an actual field-by-field extraction rehearsal essential. Do not infer that a CSV includes reward history or that a candidate can import it. Where reconstruction is unsupported, agree a retained lookup, manual honoring process or explicit replacement benefit with accountable customer service coverage.</p>
    <h2>Rehearse earning, redemption and refunds across locations</h2>
    <p>Proposed fixture, not a merchant result: a cookware retailer has an online store and two registers. A member earns on a qualifying pan, uses a reward on a later purchase, then partially returns the first order. Record the expected earned-point reversal, spent points, remaining reward and tier treatment before the demonstration. Include a refund after the balance has been spent, expiry during a return dispute and a staff correction with an audit reason.</p>
    <p>The <a class="link" href="https://help.marsello.com/how-do-i-automatically-remove-loyalty-points-for-shopify-orders-marsello-help-center">Shopify points removal guide</a> ties reversals to configured payment statuses, including proportional product value for a selected partial-refund status. Compare the actual account settings with receipt-level calculations. Separately, the <a class="link" href="https://help.marsello.com/shopify-pos-common-questions-marsello-help-center">POS FAQ</a> warns that removing a discount code does not refund points. Staff must know which action resolves a mistaken redemption.</p>
    <p>Replay an order update and verify one earning entry. Try an unauthorized register and an excluded product; compare member portal, receipt and staff view. The <a class="link" href="https://help.marsello.com/how-do-i-connect-my-shopify-site-to-marsello-marsello-help-center">Shopify site setup guide</a> treats online and POS as separately enabled sites. A shared account does not authorize every franchise, location or staff role to redeem every benefit.</p>
    <h2>Keep membership, identity and channel permission distinct</h2>
    <p>Map Shopify customer ID, POS identity, email and phone to the member ledger. Exercise a changed email, shared household phone and duplicate customer merge without silently moving another person’s benefits. Keep evidence for marketing permission by channel and brand or store scope; loyalty enrollment and an order phone number are not sufficient SMS permission.</p>
    <p>In a partial replacement, specify which system publishes points and tier changes, how the sender acknowledges them and what happens when the feed stops. Retain newer withdrawals even when an older member snapshot is replayed. At dispatch check permission, applicable local sending restrictions, benefit validity and suppression again. A reward reminder should stop after redemption or expiry; a cart message should stop after purchase. Test STOP and HELP routing for the chosen sender and a safe hold when timezone or permission is unresolved.</p>
    <h2>Preserve campaign value without inventing results</h2>
    <p>For the proposed cookware store, plan a quarterly calendar around a limited color release, gift deadline and replenishment accessory. Give interested members early access without automatically adding a discount. A first-time shopper on the exact product waitlist can be more relevant than a high-spend member with no interest in that item. Validate stock by variant and location before a scarcity message; do not reuse an old sell-through figure as urgency.</p>
    <p>Use email for care instructions, product education and gift selection where that matches the capture promise. Reserve a text for a useful access or deadline alert to eligible recipients. Separate bargain-sensitive clearance audiences from full-price loyalists, and suppress active subscription customers from irrelevant replenishment offers. Agree contact-level collision rules across reward reminders, welcome, launch and winback; choose caps from the actual promise and response data, with a stop rule for complaints and mismatched offers rather than a universal monthly quota.</p>
    <h2>Choose candidates by the layer being changed</h2>
    <p>For an SMS-only replacement, take the exact reward-trigger-to-send trace to <a class="link" href="/apps/postscript">Postscript</a> or <a class="link" href="/apps/attentive">Attentive</a>. Ask each to demonstrate the necessary inbound fields, withdrawal handling, reply ownership and queue cancellation. These are candidate jobs, not claims that either tool inherits Marsello loyalty or that a larger store must buy a managed contract.</p>
    <p>For a combined messaging replacement, evaluate <a class="link" href="/apps/omnisend">Omnisend</a> or <a class="link" href="/apps/klaviyo">Klaviyo</a> with the same member feed and actual team workflow. An email-only requirement may merit an <a class="link" href="/apps/sequenzy">email workflow evaluation</a>, but does not select Sequenzy by default. Full loyalty replacement additionally requires a demonstrated POS, refund and benefit ledger solution; no messaging candidate on this page is certified as that replacement.</p>
    <h2>Count product cost and benefit obligations once</h2>
    <p>Use a proposed order worksheet: $100 merchandise value less a $10 redeemed reward leaves $90 net sales; less $45 goods cost leaves $45 before fulfillment, payment, returns, messaging and service costs. Do not subtract the same $10 reward again. Track unredeemed points and issued benefits in a separate liability reconciliation with finance; their treatment is not necessarily cash face value or immediate profit.</p>
    <p>Compare current <a class="link" href="https://www.marsello.com/pricing">Marsello pricing</a> and written candidate quotes for the same enabled sites, billable contacts, channel usage, destinations, connectors and peak month. Include temporary overlap, staff training, benefit honoring, failed-feed reconciliation and support. For a proposed controlled trial, allocate eligible members before sends and compare contribution per assigned member against a holdout over a relevant purchase window. Subtract fixed subscription and setup at program level. Attributed revenue and a higher redemption rate alone do not establish incremental margin.</p>
    <h2>Accept partial and full replacement differently</h2>
    <p>For a channel change, retain Marsello as the agreed benefit authority and give each reminder or campaign exactly one queue owner. Record checkpoint event IDs, remaining messages and completed sends. Pause outgoing entries for an exclusive cohort before enabling the replacement. Reconcile purchases, redemptions, expiries and withdrawals that occur between snapshot and dispatch; replay acknowledged missing events without duplicating points or sends. Accept only when the customer-facing balance remains consistent and staff can resolve an exception.</p>
    <p>For a full change, additionally reconcile opening and closing ledger totals and member-level exceptions, tier qualification, issued rewards and every supported register. Communicate how customers access benefits and how staff honor disputed rewards. Keep a staffed lookup until unresolved obligations have an agreed resolution. Do not retire access simply because contact counts match.</p>
    <p>Rollback means stopping new candidate sends and ledger writes, retaining completed transactions, then reconciling all changes since the checkpoint before restoring an owner. Never restore an old balance over a legitimate redemption or resubscribe a withdrawn member. Stay or repair if no candidate clears these checks. Continue with the <a class="link" href="/apps/marsello">Marsello evaluation</a> and <a class="link" href="/guides/offer-discipline">offer discipline guide</a>.</p>
    <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
